hadiths[32]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2840","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""There is a supplication for every Prophet. I intend, if Allah wills, to conceal my supplication on the Day of Judgment for the intercession of my Ummah."""
"2841","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the same is true from this chain of transmission."
"2842","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the hadith that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Seventy thousand people from my Ummah will go to Paradise without reckoning"", Sayyidna 'Akasha (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray that Allah make me one of those people. He prayed. Another person said: Pray for me too. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Akasha has prevailed over you."""
"2843","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi al-Judaa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “With the intercession of a man from my Ummah, more people than Banutamim will enter Paradise.” The people said: “Except you, O Messenger of Allah!” He said: “Yes, except me.”"
"2844","Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, said: I asked the mother of the believers, Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with her: What do you think about the saying of Allah: ""The day the earth will be changed to the earth and the heavens..."" (Ibrahim: 48/14), where will the people be on that day? Translation: On the day when the earth will be replaced except for this earth and the heavens, and all of them will face Allah Wahid wa Khar (One and Mighty Dominant). Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) about this, and he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) said: (At that time, people will be on the bridge)."
"2845","Sidi, may God have mercy on him, said: I once heard this verse from Marah (Hamdani): . . . . . ﴾» (Maryam: 71/19) asked the meaning: (i.e.: There is none of you who will not enter the Hellfire), Marah narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrated a hadith to him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All people will enter the Hellfire, then they will come out of it according to their deeds, so the first person will come out like a flash of lightning, then the second like the wind, and the third like the running of a fast horse. The fourth like a camel-rider, and the fifth like a man running, the sixth like a man walking."""
"2846","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, death will be brought in the form of a gray ram and it will be made to stand between Paradise and Hell, then it will be called: O people of Paradise! Then they will look with their necks raised, then it will be said: They will look at him with their necks raised and understand that the time for redemption has come, at that time (at this time) (the ram meaning death) will be slaughtered and it will be said: Now live forever, death will not come.”"
"2847","Sayyidina Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) giving a sermon. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated this word again and again, even if all the people in the market were present in my place, they would have listened, and while saying this, the cloak of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell at his feet."
"2848","Bahz bin Hakeem narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There was a servant of Allah who did not believe in any religion. He said: Very good father! He said: I will not leave my property with you, unless I give you an order, then he took a promise from them, he said: When I die, take me in the fire and when I am burnt, then throw my ashes in the air. He said: ""By my Lord! These boys did the same to him after he died. He was brought to his original state and presented before the Lord of the Worlds. Allah Almighty said: What prompted you to take fire? He said: Your fear, O my Lord. Allah Almighty said: I see you afraid"", he said: ""He Repentance was accepted. (i.e. he was forgiven). 
 Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""Yabtair"" means ""Yaddakhir"" meaning what has been stored for the hereafter."
"2849","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman went to Hell because of a cat. It was said to her, 'You did not feed it, did not water it, and did not let it go (but kept it tied up) so that it would have eaten the insects of the earth.'"""
"2850","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ninety-nine dragons will be imposed on the unbeliever in his grave, which will scratch and bite him until the Day of Judgment comes. If one of them blows into the ground, no grass will grow from the ground."""
"2851","Muhammad bin Wasee said: I went to Bilal bin Abi Barda, I said: Your father narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There is a valley in Hell called Habhab, every rebellious and arrogant person will stay in it, beware that you are not one of those people."
"2852","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But those who are in Hell (i.e. are destined to stay there forever, like infidels and polytheists), they will not die in Hell, and some of the people will be such (disobedient) that the fire will catch them according to their sins and they will burn in it until they become coals, then they will be ordered to intercede, so they will be removed from Hell in groups. They will come out and spread in the rivers of Paradise, and it will be said to the people of Paradise: Pour water on them."" He said: ""So the people of Paradise will pour water on those who come from Hell, from which their flesh will grow as a grain grows and flourishes in the flow of water (ie, they will recover very quickly)."""
"2853","On the authority of Sayyidina Abdullah bin Masoud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There are eight gates to Paradise."""
"2854","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He who goes to Paradise will enjoy himself, he will not have any sorrow, nor will his clothes rot, nor will his youth decline (ie, he will remain young forever, he will not grow old) and for him there will be things in Paradise that no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has even thought of it."""
"2855","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Paradise, the place of the lash of one of you is better than the world and whatever is in the world. If you wish, recite this verse: ""Famin zuhziha anni al-Naar . On the Day of Resurrection, you will be given your full reward, so whoever is removed from the Fire, and admitted to Paradise, he has certainly succeeded, and the worldly life is only a deception."
"2856","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: We asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): How is Paradise built? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""A brick of gold and a brick of silver, the slurry is musk azfar, and its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its soil is saffron. Whoever enters it will be luxurious, he will not have any sorrow or boredom, nor will their youth perish there, nor will their clothes (of Paradise) grow old."""
"2857","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qays narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are four Jannahs of Al-Firdus, two Jannahs of gold, they and their ornaments (ornaments) and vessels and whatever is in them are all of gold, and two Jannahs of silver, their ornaments, vessels and everything are of silver, and there in the Jannahs of Eden there will be only a veil of gravel on the face of Allah between the people and the sight of Allah, and these rivers and jinns. It originates from Aden and later falls into the canals through pits.” 
 Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Juba, by which the journey of the earth can be completed."
"2858","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""The first group of my ummah who will enter Paradise will have faces as bright as the fourteenth moon, then the group that will enter after them will be like the brightest stars in the sky."" Ask Allah Ta'ala to make me one of them. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Allah, make Akasha one of them."" Pray for me too, may Allah make me one of them."
"2859","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira and Sayyidna Abu Saeed (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): . . . . . . .﴾» (Al-A'raf: 43/7) Translation: (And they will be called that this paradise has been given to you in return for your deeds), the meaning of this verse is that they will be called and said: It has been decreed for you to be healthy, and you will never get sick, enjoy luxury, you will not have any sorrow and grief, stay young, do not grow old and live forever, never die."
"2860","Sayyidna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man in Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, sexual intercourse, and sexual intercourse."" Hearing this, a Jew said: ""Whoever eats and drinks needs to relieve himself?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(Instead of talking) sweat will come out of his skin, which will shrink his stomach (ie, there will be no need for bowel movements)."""
"2861","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The people of Paradise are bald men with gray hair, their clothes will not be torn, and their youth will not perish."""
"2862","On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, Abu Asim was asked: Did he narrate it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, the people of Paradise will neither urinate nor sneeze nor defecate, instead they will burp, eat, drink and will be inspired by Tasbeeh and Tahamid like the inspiration of breath."
"2863","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Allah, the Exalted and Exalted, says: I have prepared for My pious servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has ever imagined. (Sajdah 17/32) Translation: No one knows what We have kept hidden from them, the coldness of their eyes, and what they used to do is its recompense."
"2864","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The lowest level of Paradise will be the one who wishes to Allah and it will be said to him: You have as much as you wished for and more like it, and he will be told (there is a tradition to exhort him) to ask for such and such, and in response it will be said to him: This is what he asked for and more like it for you."" 
 Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""It will be said to him: This and ten times like it is for you."""
"2865","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The people of Paradise will see the people of one upper room and the other upper rooms as you see the star in the sky (i.e. they will be so high and far from each other due to the difference in degrees)."" Narrated and they said: As you see the Kukab Dari in the sky on the eastern or western edge."
"2866","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to Paradise will have two wives, the pulp of whose thighs (because of their beauty) will be visible even under seventy clothes, and there will be no wife in Paradise."""
"2867","On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qays, his father said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""In Paradise there will be a tent of hollow pearl, its length will be sixty miles, and on each side of it there will be a wife of a Muslim who will not be seen by others."""
"2868","On the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When a believer wishes for a child in Paradise, his pregnancy, pregnancy and growing up (i.e. age) will all be according to his wish in one hour."""
"2869","Sulaiman bin Barida, I believe, narrating from his father, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There will be one hundred and twenty rows of the people of Paradise, of which this row will be for my Ummah and forty rows will be for all the other (ummah) people."""
"2870","Hakeem bin Muawiya narrated from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""In Paradise there is a sea of milk, a sea of honey, and a sea of wine, then rivers flow from them."""
"2871","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: When “Inna Aatinaka Al-Kawthar” was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “It is a river of Paradise, the banks of which are made of gold, it flows on pearls and rubies, its soil is more fragrant than musk, and its taste is sweeter than honey, and its water is whiter (and transparent) than snow.”"
